I have all the exact declarations from `safevalues@1.2.0`'s `.d.ts` files in `node_modules`.

**1. sanitizeHtml** — `from 'safevalues'` (`dist/mjs/builders/html_sanitizer/html_sanitizer.d.ts`):
```ts
export declare function sanitizeHtml(html: string): SafeHtml;
```
Takes only `html: string` — no options/config argument. It uses a fixed default sanitizer configuration (no allowed-tags/attrs param). For custom configs, `HtmlSanitizerBuilder`/`CssSanitizerBuilder` exist, and `sanitizeHtmlAssertUnchanged(html: string): SafeHtml` / `sanitizeHtmlToFragment(html: string): DocumentFragment` are siblings, also default-only.

**2. setElementInnerHtml** — `from 'safevalues/dom'` (`dist/mjs/dom/elements/element.d.ts`):
```ts
declare type ScriptOrStyle = HTMLScriptElement | HTMLStyleElement | SVGScriptElement | SVGStyleElement;
export declare function setElementInnerHtml<T extends Element | ShadowRoot>(elOrRoot: Exclude<T, ScriptOrStyle>, v: SafeHtml): void;
```
Accepts `Element | ShadowRoot` (generic, excluding script/style elements), not `HTMLElement` specifically.

**3. setAnchorHref** — `from 'safevalues/dom'` (`dist/mjs/dom/elements/anchor.d.ts`):
```ts
export declare function setAnchorHref(anchor: HTMLAnchorElement, url: Url): void;
```
where `Url = string` (type alias, from `builders/url_builders.js`).

**4. setLocationHref** — `from 'safevalues/dom'` (`dist/mjs/dom/globals/location.d.ts`):
```ts
export declare function setLocationHref(loc: Location, url: Url): void;
```
(siblings `locationReplace`/`locationAssign` have identical signature shape).

**5. SafeHtml type** — `from 'safevalues'` (`dist/mjs/internals/html_impl.d.ts`), exported directly by name (re-exported via top-level `index.d.ts`):
```ts
export declare class SafeHtml {
    private readonly privateDoNotAccessOrElseWrappedHtml;
    private constructor();
    toString(): string;
}
export declare const EMPTY_HTML: SafeHtml;
export declare function isHtml(value: unknown): value is SafeHtml;
export declare function unwrapHtml(value: SafeHtml): UnwrapType<TrustedHTML> | string;
```
No separate `TrustedHtml` wrapper type is exported by name; `SafeHtml` is the wrapper class itself (constructor is private, can't be constructed directly), and `unwrapHtml` returns the underlying native `TrustedHTML` (or plain `string` if Trusted Types are disabled).

